Configure the Android slicing library without desktop UI and transports.

The Android host owns Compose/renderer UI, networking and the engine process.
Reject GUI/tools/Sentry configurations, omit desktop executable/MQTT/HID targets,
and keep curl/OpenGL dependencies out of this engine build. Retain the actual
geometry, image and CAD libraries. OCCT already has an Android font path without
fontconfig, so do not add the desktop fontconfig link. Use the tested shared TBB
runtime alongside static geometry libraries.

Read OpenVDB's ABI from its installed generated header during Android discovery.
The target vdb_print executable cannot run on the build host, and inference from
an unavailable result can silently select the wrong ABI.

Retire these branches when the pinned upstream supports a standalone Android
libslic3r target with equivalent dependency and ownership boundaries.
The WaveOverhangs source list belongs to the shared engine patch selected by
this recipe. Non-Android dependency and executable guards remain unchanged.

---
